[QUESTION 46]
The correct order of increasing boiling points of the following compounds \text{C}_3\text{H}_7\text{OH}, \text{C}_7\text{H}_{16} and \text{C}_4\text{H}_{10} is
A. \text{C}_3\text{H}_7\text{OH} \rightarrow \text{C}_4\text{H}_{10} \rightarrow \text{C}_7\text{H}_{16}
B. \text{C}_4\text{H}_{10} \rightarrow \text{C}_7\text{H}_{16} \rightarrow \text{C}_3\text{H}_7\text{OH}
C. \text{C}_7\text{H}_{16} \rightarrow \text{C}_3\text{H}_7\text{OH} \rightarrow \text{C}_4\text{H}_{10}
D. \text{C}_4\text{H}_{10} \rightarrow \text{C}_3\text{H}_7\text{OH} \rightarrow \text{C}_7\text{H}_{16}
Answer Key: D
Explanation:
 * \text{C}_4\text{H}_{10} (butane) is a short non-polar alkane with weak van der Waals forces, giving it the lowest boiling point.
 * \text{C}_3\text{H}_7\text{OH} (propanol) contains an -\text{OH} group capable of strong intermolecular hydrogen bonding, raising its boiling point.
 * \text{C}_7\text{H}_{16} (heptane) is a much larger hydrocarbon with a significantly higher molar mass and extensive dispersion forces.
 * Ordering by strength of intermolecular forces gives \text{C}_4\text{H}_{10} < \text{C}_3\text{H}_7\text{OH} < \text{C}_7\text{H}_{16}, matching option D.

[QUESTION 81]
The functional group present in alkenes is
A. \text{C}\equiv\text{C}
B. \text{C}=\text{C}
C. \text{C}-\text{C}
D. -\text{OH}
Answer Key: B
Explanation:
 * Alkenes are unsaturated hydrocarbons containing at least one carbon-carbon double bond (\text{C}=\text{C}).
 * Alkanes contain carbon-carbon single bonds (\text{C}-\text{C}).
 * Alkynes contain carbon-carbon triple bonds (\text{C}\equiv\text{C}).
 * Therefore, \text{C}=\text{C} is the signature functional group of alkenes.

[QUESTION 83]
The standard condition for temperature and pressure (STP) defines temperature and pressure as
A. 25^\circ\text{C} and 1\text{ atm}
B. 0^\circ\text{C} and 1\text{ atm}
C. 100^\circ\text{C} and 760\text{ mmHg}
D. 273\text{ K} and 10\text{ atm}
Answer Key: B
Explanation:
 * Standard Temperature and Pressure (STP) is defined as 0^\circ\text{C} (273.15\text{ K}) and 1\text{ atm} (760\text{ mmHg} / 101.3\text{ kPa}).
 * Under STP conditions, 1 mole of an ideal gas occupies a molar volume of 22.4\text{ dm}^3.
 * Thus, option B states the correct STP parameters.
